# The all-wac mode's settings (wacuum + the light-client driver). Kept across reinstalls; edit, then
# systemctl restart wacuum-driver.

# Any beacon node serving the light-client API and blocks over HTTPS. It is trusted for nothing — every update is
# checked by signature and branch, every block by its proven hash — but it must answer: pick one that does, or two
# and switch on failure. A public one rate-limits; the driver backs off.
BEACON_URL=https://lodestar-mainnet.chainsafe.io
# A beacon block root trusted from outside, for the first start only (later starts use the finalized root the
# driver verified and kept). Take it from somewhere you trust: a checkpoint-sync provider you choose, a friend's
# node, a block explorer, more than one of them agreeing. https://eth-clients.github.io/checkpoint-sync-endpoints/
CHECKPOINT=

# wacuum's own (docs/mainnet.md, "Memory on the 32 GB box"): the V8 heap, the store's entry cache, and how many
# finalized blocks of history it holds in memory (~320 KB each on mainnet).
WAC_MAX_HEAP=6g
CACHE_MB=1536
HISTORY=1024
# Mainnet's execution-layer bootnodes (go-ethereum 1.17.10's params/bootnodes.go), for peers to snap-sync from; space-separated.
BOOTNODES="enode://d860a01f9722d78051619d1e2351aba3f43f943f6f00718d1b9baa4101932a1f5011f16bb2b1bb35db20d6fe28fa0bf09636d26a87d31de9ec6203eeedb1f666@18.138.108.67:30303 enode://22a8232c3abc76a16ae9d6c3b164f98775fe226f0917b0ca871128a74a8e9630b458460865bab457221f1d448dd9791d24c4e5d88786180ac185df813a68d4de@3.209.45.79:30303 enode://2b252ab6a1d0f971d9722cb839a42cb81db019ba44c08754628ab4a823487071b5695317c8ccd085219c3a03af063495b2f1da8d18218da2d6a82981b45e6ffc@65.108.70.101:30303 enode://4aeb4ab6c14b23e2c4cfdce879c04b0748a20d8e9b59e25ded2a08143e265c6c25936e74cbc8e641e3312ca288673d91f2f93f8e277de3cfa444ecdaaf982052@157.90.35.166:30303"
